51:     """
52:     Slide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.
53: 
54:     Input structure
55:     - The background is the dominant color.
56:     - The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.
57:     - One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.
58:     - Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.
59: 
60:     Rule
61:     - Clear the extra objects from their original positions.
62:     - For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.
63:     - Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.
64:     - Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.
65: 
66:     Key insight
67:     - The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.
68:     """
